<title>SWITZERLAND: SIG posts higher 1996 net, ups dividend.</title>
<headline>SIG posts higher 1996 net, ups dividend.</headline>
<dateline>NEUHAUSEN, Switzerland 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Calendar 1996</p>
<p>				    (million Sfr unless stated)</p>
<p> Group net			88.6		vs 70.1</p>
<p> Operating profit	     118.4	     vs 102.3</p>
<p> Sales			    1,640.4	   vs 1,637.6</p>
<p> Cash flow			191.1	     vs 170.3</p>
<p> Div (bearer, Sfr)	    60		  vs 50</p>
<p> Div (regd, Sfr)		30		  vs 25</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of Swiss mechanical engineering group is SIG Schweizerische Industrie-Gesellschaft Holding AG. An SIG statement said 1995 sales included railroad car division which was divested as of January 1, 1996.</p>
<p>SIG said the increase in operating and net profit stemmed from cost reduction.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
